-- Q11397: State and Local Government [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB 54 (par. 30), a special revenue fund accounts for proceeds of specific revenue sources restricted or committed to specified purposes. When the state repeals the fuel tax allocation, the specific revenue source justifying the fund''s existence is eliminated, so the fund should be closed or reclassified.
Wrong (A): A fund does not continue simply because it was properly established. The defining criterion is the ongoing existence of a restricted or committed revenue source.
Wrong (C): There is no automatic conversion mechanism to a permanent fund. Permanent funds require legally restricted principal with only earnings available for use.
Wrong (D): A positive fund balance alone does not justify continuing a special revenue fund. The specific restricted or committed revenue source is the defining characteristic.$EXPL$
