  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GASB 34, a permanent fund accounts for resources legally restricted so that only earnings--not principal--may be used for the government''s own programs. Because the endowment benefits the city''s library programs (a governmental purpose), it belongs in a permanent fund.
Wrong (A): A special revenue fund accounts for restricted revenue streams, not endowment principal that must be permanently invested.
Wrong (B): A private-purpose trust fund would apply if beneficiaries were external parties rather than government programs.
Wrong (C): The general fund is for unrestricted resources. This endowment has specific legal restrictions on both principal and earnings use.$EXPL$
