-- Q11430: State and Local Government [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under GASB 34 (par. 22-26), capital assets with indefinite or inexhaustible useful lives are not depreciated. Land has an inexhaustible useful life, and construction in progress is not yet placed in service, so neither is subject to depreciation.
Wrong (B): Buildings and improvements have finite useful lives and must be depreciated under GASB 34.
Wrong (C): Infrastructure assets reported under the depreciation approach are, by definition, being depreciated over their estimated useful lives.
Wrong (D): Equipment and vehicles have finite useful lives and are depreciated under standard capital asset accounting.$EXPL$
