-- Q11432: State and Local Government [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB Interpretation No. 1, bond anticipation notes meeting take-out financing criteria are excluded from governmental fund liabilities and reported only in government-wide statements as long-term debt. If take-out criteria are unmet, the BANs remain as a fund liability in the capital projects fund.
Wrong (A): Governmental funds do not report long-term liabilities on the fund balance sheet. Long-term debt appears only in the government-wide statements.
Wrong (C): BANs are not automatically classified as other financing sources. They must first be evaluated against take-out criteria to determine proper classification.
Wrong (D): BANs are debt instruments, not deferred inflows of resources. Deferred inflows represent resource acquisitions applicable to future periods.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11432;

