-- Q11434: State and Local Government [hard/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under GASB 18 (par. 8-9), the closure and postclosure liability is calculated based on the percentage of capacity used: (2,600,000 / 4,000,000) x $18,000,000 = $11,700,000. The liability reflects cumulative usage regardless of restricted investments held separately.
Wrong (B): $7,500,000 incorrectly subtracts the $4,200,000 restricted investments from the computed liability. GASB 18 requires the liability and restricted assets to be reported independently.
Wrong (C): $18,000,000 represents total estimated costs, but the liability is proportional to capacity used (65%), not 100%.
Wrong (D): $13,800,000 does not correspond to any valid calculation based on the capacity percentage or the restricted investment offset.$EXPL$
